abels do not establish numerical pH, temperature, pressure, concentrations or residence times. Mixing, cooling and UV shielding are appropriately acknowledged, but fluid composition, buffering capacity, transfer losses and retention of volatile surface reagents need specification. The final equations correctly represent equilibration of racemic populations into L- and D-alanine, not stereoselective formation. L-alanine production is therefore plausible as part of a racemate; enantiopure isolation is neither demonstrated nor required for this assessment. No research findings or reaction-level citations are supplied for a detailed literature audit. Optional photochemical supply is less certain without invalidating the accepted-feedstock routes. Confidence reflects shared chemical evidence, not the number of enumerated alternatives. The network does not meet the required 0.90 overall approval threshold.\n- Issues: [\"Pyruvic-acid photodecarboxylation is balanced and can provide a plausible acetaldehyde channel, but aqueous photochemistry is sensitive to irradiation, speciation, oxygen and competing reactions. Useful acetaldehyde production and capture are therefore not established by rxn_001. Downstream chemistry retains P1's strengths and hydrolysis uncertainties. This optional source does not undermine routes using the accepted acetaldehyde feedstock.\", 'The route is stoichiometrically valid, but productive photochemical acetaldehyde supply, lactonitrile-pool turnover and alkaline hydrolysis all need condition-matched support. Lactonitrile capture could help retain acetaldehyde, but its effectiveness during or after irradiation is not demonstrated. Final alaninate protonation is chemically valid and yields L-alanine together with D-alanine.']\n\n============================================================\nAddress the above issues in your new network. Do NOT repeat the same mistakes.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"L-Alanine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"Use supplied acetaldehyde, cyanide and ammonia for Strecker chemistry, with direct capture and a reversible lactonitrile reservoir as alternative entry routes. Resolve aminonitrile hydrolysis into hydration and amide hydrolysis, with explicitly different acidic and alkaline operating histories. Eight pathways enumerate these combinations; they are not eight independent prebiotic mechanisms. Two additional pathways start from supplied pyruvic acid and use consumed native iron for direct reductive amination or oxime reduction. No selective CO2-to-pyruvate synthesis, unspecified H2-activation catalyst, hydantoin-release step or photochemical acetaldehyde source is assumed. All productive routes are achiral and yield L-alanine together with D-alanine; enantiopure isolation is not claimed. The numerical conditions below are proposed operating windows, not reported yields or demonstrations of complete environmental sequences. Mixed-pH staging, concentrated alkaline hydrolysis and direct ammonium/iron amination remain conditional. Surface chemistry requires UV-shielded porewater and retention of volatile reagents. Hydrothermal processing requires separate, chemically characterized fluids rather than an unspecified change of environment. Intermediate formulas use analytical parent forms where rapid protonation equilibria are implicit; terminal alanine charge states are represented explicitly. Coefficients are written in mechanism descriptions rather than repeated molecule IDs.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_001\",\n      \"formula\": \"C2H4O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Ethanal\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Acetaldehyde\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C2H4O/c1-2-3/h2H,1H3\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_002\",\n      \"formula\": \"CHN\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/CHN/c1-2/h1H\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_003\",\n      \"formula\": \"H3N\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Azane\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Ammonia\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/H3N/h1H3\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_004\",\n      \"formula\": \"H2O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Oxidane\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Water\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/H2O/h1H2\",\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_005\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H5NO\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-Hydroxypropanenitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Lactonitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_006\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H6N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-Aminopropanenitrile\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Alanine nitrile\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"hub_intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_007\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H8N2O\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-Aminopropanamide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Alaninamide\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"hub_intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_008\",\n      \"formula\": \"H+\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Hydron\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Aqueous proton equivalent\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_009\",\n      \"formula\": \"HO-\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Hydroxide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Hydroxide ion\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_010\",\n      \"formula\": \"H4N+\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"Azanium\",\n      \"common_name\": \"Ammonium\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_011\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H8NO2+\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(1S)-1-Carboxyethan-1-aminium\",\n      \"common_name\": \"L-Alaninium\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_012\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H8NO2+\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(1R)-1-Carboxyethan-1-aminium\",\n      \"common_name\": \"D-Alaninium\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_013\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H6NO2-\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(2S)-2-Aminopropanoate\",\n      \"common_name\": \"L-Alaninate\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_014\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H6NO2-\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(2R)-2-Aminopropanoate\",\n      \"common_name\": \"D-Alaninate\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Hydrothermal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_015\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H7NO2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(2S)-2-Aminopropanoic acid\",\n      \"common_name\": \"L-Alanine\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C3H7NO2/c1-2(4)3(5)6/h2H,4H2,1H3,(H,5,6)/t2-/m0/s1\",\n      \"role\": \"target\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_016\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H7NO2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"(2R)-2-Aminopropanoic acid\",\n      \"common_name\": \"D-Alanine\",\n      \"inchi\": \"InChI=1S/C3H7NO2/c1-2(4)3(5)6/h2H,4H2,1H3,(H,5,6)/t2-/m1/s1\",\n      \"role\": \"intermediate\",\n      \"environment_formed\": \"Surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_017\",\n      \"formula\": \"C3H4O3\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"2-Oxop